#: ../../source/validation/report/index.rst:5
msgid ""
"What this repository's :doc:`validation documents <../index>` claim, "
"gathered into one place. The figures below are a *summary of claims*, not"
" a proof of them: they say who has vouched for which files under which "
"methodology, and whether the signatures and hashes still hold as of the "
"run that wrote this page. To be sure of any line of it, run the check "
"yourself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/report/index.rst:14
msgid ""
"The assertions this repository grants are the prose ones under "
"``docs/source/validation/assertions/`` — statements about the software "
"that a person read, understood and agreed with, recorded under "
":doc:`agreement and good faith "
"<../methodologies/agreement_and_good_faith>`. A grant of one of them is a"
" claim about a *statement*, not about any bytes a program wrote, which is"
" what separates it from the methodologies a formats repository uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/report/index.rst:21
msgid "`Open the coverage page: the three viewpoints as tabs <../coverage.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/report/index.rst:25
msgid ""
"That page is a single generated HTML file published beside this site, the"
" same arrangement the :doc:`Rust API <../../generated/rust-api>` uses. It"
" is **not** rebuilt with the site: whether a signature is valid is "
"computed from the keyring of whoever runs the command, and a "
"documentation builder has no public keys in it — so a page generated "
"there would announce that every grant in the repository is invalid. It is"
" written by the commit hook, on a machine that holds the keys, and "
"committed under ``docs/source/_extra/validation/``. Building the site "
"only copies it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/report/index.rst:35
msgid ""
"1 grant by 1 contributor under 1 methodology; coverage 1/1 (100%); check-"
"grants: passing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/report/index.rst:37
msgid ""
"*Generated by `freeports-validate report`, and demonstrative: it shows "
"what this repository's validation documents claim as of one run, not that"
" the data is correct. To be sure of any line, run `freeports-validate "
"check-grants` yourself.* `What these claims are worth: the general "
"methodology "
"<https://docs.freeports.org/en/stable/validation/general_methodology.html>`_."
msgstr ""

